Package: thermify
Title: Efficient Agroclimatic Thermal Indices
Version: 0.3.1.9000
Authors@R: person("Guillermo", "Fuentes-Jaque", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "gfuentesj@correo.uss.cl",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7864-4899"))
Description: Computes growing degree-days (average, single and double sine,
    single and double triangle methods with horizontal, vertical and
    intermediate cutoffs; Allen (1976) <doi:10.1093/ee/5.3.388>),
    degree-hours, chilling hours, Utah model chill units (Richardson et al.
    1974) and Dynamic model chill portions (Fishman et al. (1987)
    <doi:10.1016/S0022-5193(87)80237-0>) from daily or hourly temperatures.
    Monthly climatologies such as 'WorldClim' 2.1 (Fick and Hijmans (2017)
    <doi:10.1002/joc.5086>) can be densified to daily values with a
    mean-preserving interpolation, natively or through the 'tempify' Python
    package, and then to hourly values with sine or Linvill (1990)
    <doi:10.21273/HORTSCI.25.1.14> diurnal models. Raster workflows based on
    'terra' process data in blocks. Outputs based on monthly climatologies
    are model-based estimates, not observations.
